## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design privacy-preserving ML pipelines across tenants with governance constraints. It also probes how to coordinate training, model registry, and DR while controlling cost.

## Key Concepts
- Federated learning across tenants
- Azure ML orchestration and Delta Lake
- Purview RBAC BYOK governance
- Drift monitoring and auditability
- DR and cost optimization

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for federated training loop
function train_round(tenant_config, local_data_uri, model, aggregator_uri){
  const local_model = train(model, load(local_data_uri));
  const update = compute_update(local_model, model);
  send_update_to_server(aggregator_uri, update);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you detect and respond to drift across tenants?
- How would you handle non-IID data and stragglers in the federation?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a novice-level Azure native onboarding pattern with tenant isolation, governance, encryption, and cost discipline.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant resource scoping (RG, storage, Synapse)
- Delta Lake on ADLS Gen2, Purview tagging, RBAC
- BYOK via Key Vault, tenant keys
- Data Factory ingestion and autoscale; simple retention

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: create tenant resources and assign RBAC
const tenantId = "tenant-123";
await createResourceGroup(`rg-${tenantId}`);
await createAdlsGen2(`storage-${tenantId}`, { enableHierarchicalNamespace: true });
await createSynapseWorkspace(`synapse-${tenantId}`);
await assignRole(`reader`, `principal-${tenantId}`, `rbac-${tenantId}`);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test onboarding for a new tenant with key rotation?
- How would you scale this pattern to thousands of tenants while maintaining isolation?

